\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{frap}

\taxon{Example}
\title{Corner twists and edge flips on the cube}

\p{Use the unmarked-center, fixed-frame sticker model of
\vocabk{one cube face turn}{frap-000P}. We apply the canonical character of
\citet{Section 3.1, p. 7}{marchetti2025rubik} to this explicit action.
At a corner the three incident sticker directions have a cyclic order
inherited from the ambient orientation. Choose bijective cyclic frames
at all eight positions. Rotations preserve that order, giving local group
#{C_3}; at each of the twelve edges an ordering of its two stickers gives
local group #{C_2}. Both actions on the local stickers are faithful.
Writing these groups additively, the two characters are}
##{\chi_c=\sum_{i=1}^{8}a_i\pmod3,\qquad
      \chi_e=\sum_{j=1}^{12}b_j\pmod2.}

\p{A quarter-turn has one four-cycle of affected corners and one of
affected edges. Four applications restore every sticker, so the return
transport on each of these cycles is the identity. Every other corner
and edge is fixed with identity local transport. The
[cycle criterion](frap-000U) gives #{\chi_c=0} and #{\chi_e=0}
for every face quarter-turn. The [kernel argument](frap-000T) extends
this to every word in those turns, including inverses and half-turns.}

\p{For a concrete cyclic frame, choose any frame at corner #{i_0} of
the upper face and define the next three by transporting it with the
shape rotation #{q}. Since #{q^4=1}, all four local factors of this
turn become zero. This frame checks that one generator; the
[frame-independence theorem](frap-000S) transfers the conclusion to
any fixed choice of cyclic frames used for the other generators.}

\p{A configuration with a \newvocab{corner twist} of just one corner by #{1} has
#{\chi_c=1} and is impossible under these moves. Twisting two corners
by #{1} and #{-1} passes this test, but the calculation alone does not
construct a legal sequence. Likewise, flipping exactly one edge fails
the second test. An \newvocab{edge flip} of exactly one edge therefore
fails the second test. Reachability needs additional arguments.}
